sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0253, drained Node reboots one at a time; docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#fleet-reboot.
  %% status: draft
  %% kind: fleet.reboot
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Pick Nodes<br/>in risk order
  %%> When:
  %%> - every day at 03:06 Europe/Amsterdam, after the rollout admission; the window is 03:00–06:00
  %%> - when an operator posts to `fleet/reboot`; that pass ignores the window
  %%> - always while `ORBIT_FLEET_REBOOT` is on (the default)
  %%> Picks:
  %%> - every active Linux Node with a WireGuard address and a pinned host key, except task VMs
  %%> - in the rollout's groups, then the control path (`vpn` hub, Gateway, `swamp.orbit` Node), then the `swamp` Node
  %%> - a reboot hold is frozen as `defer: operator_hold`; a held Node is read but never drained or rebooted
  %%> - a task host with open task work is read and reported `deferred` (`tasks_busy`)
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other pass, no fleet rollout and no Gateway release runs; they refuse each other
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-reboot
  %%> While it runs:
  %%> - task calls for its task hosts refuse with `tasks.host_rebooting`; placement and image refresh skip them
  loop each Node, one at a time
    SW->>N: Drain the Node<br/>drain phase
    %%> Why:
    %%> - only the initial safe boot-state reads retry SSH exit 255: eight attempts, 10 s each, with Ansible backoff (0, 1, 3, 7, 15, 30, 30 s); at most 166 s before overhead
    %%> - drain, stops and reboot use zero SSH retries; a disconnect after execution never replays the command
    %%> - a held Node that cannot be read fails and halts the pass, as any other Node does
    %%> - after a failed Node: `skipped`; outside the window: `deferred`; no `/var/run/reboot-required`: `not_due`
    %%> - a due held Node records boot ID, kernel and due time, then `deferred` (`operator_hold`); without a due reboot it stays `not_due`
    %%> - CI: stop each idle runner, frozen while read; a job still running after 15 min defers the Node
    %%> - task guests stop and are recorded parked; on the Gateway the scheduler stops and Horizon drains within 15 min
    %%> - record `drain_started` before the first stop; rescue runs the existing Gateway and CI recovery only after that marker
    SW->>N: Reboot and wait for SSH<br/>reboot phase
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the swamp Node instead schedules its own reboot after the run ends: `scheduled`
    SW->>N: Check the new boot<br/>check phase
    %%> Checks:
    %%> - new boot ID, newest kernel, nothing due, no newly failed unit, agent, Gateway scheduler and Horizon, hub tunnel and source unit active
    opt a CI host whose drain stopped runners
      SW->>GW: Mint Actions write tokens<br/>github-token
      %%> Why:
      %%> - one `actions: write` token per Project repository, from the App's existing permission; no runner administration (ADR 0223)
      SW->>SW: Re-run lost CI jobs<br/>rerun phase
      %%> Picks:
      %%> - failed jobs a stopped runner was still running at its freeze; never a cancelled run
      %%> - `rerun-failed-jobs` once, only while the run is still at that attempt; the Node's result lists them
    end
    SW->>SW: Record phase failures<br/>Record the Node
    %%> Why:
    %%> - always on the controller, including after UNREACHABLE bypasses Ansible rescue
    %%> - private JSON callback reports supply `failed` / `fleet.node_unreachable` and bounded redacted SSH diagnostic text
    %%> - a started phase without a terminal report or Node outcome is `failed` / `fleet.reboot_cut`; `not_reached` needs an earlier recorded halt
  end
  alt every Node rebooted, scheduled, not due, deferred or skipped
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>each Node's outcome
    %%> Result:
    %%> - every Node result shows `reboot_hold` as admitted; held task hosts keep taking work
    %%> - the Gateway records parked task VMs; a Node due for more than 3 days raises `reboot_overdue`
  else a Node fails or has unknown outcome
    SW--xGW: Pass failed<br/>outcomes · error_code
    %%> Why stop:
    %%> - without a Node report, the Gateway records `unknown` / `run_interrupted`, fails the pass and alerts once
    %%> - missing records before a recorded halt stay unknown; only Nodes after that halt may be `not_reached`
    %%> - after a recorded Node failure, later Nodes record `skipped` / `halted` without SSH; the next pass starts again there
    Note over GW: Alert once<br/>reboot_halted
  end
  Note over GW: Confirm 209 boot<br/>from its uptime
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - 30 minutes after the pass without a new boot: `reboot_unconfirmed`
